@page "/"

<PageTitle>Aspire Messages MVP</PageTitle>

<h1>Messages overview / detail</h1>

<p>
    Baseline Aspire app with a <strong>backend Api</strong> and a <strong>Blazor Server</strong>
    frontend. The first scenario is a messages inbox: list → detail → change state → back to overview.
</p>

<p>
    Later scenarios (navigation strategies, stale list state, browser back, multi-tab, etc.)
    can share this same shell.
</p>

<ol>
    <li>Start: <code>dotnet run --project AppHost</code></li>
    <li>Open <a href="http://127.0.0.1:5300/messages">http://127.0.0.1:5300/messages</a></li>
    <li>Click a message, change its state, then use <strong>Back to overview</strong>.</li>
</ol>

<p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="messages">Open messages</a></p>
